{
 "poem": "I am Gill\nI am James\nI am an artist\na Cree voice rising\nweaving sound into the unseen\nIndigenous kin, my culture’s pulse\nvisual arts\nFine art and music\nare rivers I swim, a daily drift\na lifelong hum\nArtistry a starfield I chase\nAll my relations,\nin all my creations\ntheir breath in every chord I make and everything\nI create.\nᑕᐣᓯ",
 "bio": "∞ ᑕᐣᓯ James Gill is a Canadian indigenous multidisciplinary artist.  He blends visual storytelling with sustainable, nature-focused design, and thought provoking imagery and movement. His artful eye and practical nature creates immersive design that fuse art, natural materials, and functionality, redefining spaces + experiences with a culturally resonant human-centred perspective.  Known for evocative visual artistry, lighting innovation, practical tactile design, and lofi chillpop music with dreamy acoustic duets and lulling rhythms. Gill's passion for coffee, fine arts, music + urban design reflects a deep connection with nature",
